Subject: server: don't load the draft model when no speculator will use it

has_dft() only checked that a draft model path/repo was configured, so the
server loaded the drafter even when speculation is disabled. With a plain
draft model that just wastes memory (types defaults to {NONE} and no
speculative impl consumes the context). With an MTP assistant gguf it
crashes: the drafter is loaded as a regular draft context (the MTP context
type is only set when draft-mtp is among the enabled types), and building
a normal graph for the head-only MTP checkpoint asserts at
llama-graph.cpp "missing result_norm/result_embd tensor".

Hit in practice by our packaged llamafile, whose baked-in .args pass
"-md /zip/mtp-....gguf --spec-type draft-mtp": with the 0012 patch a user
appending "--spec-type none" correctly resets the type list, but the
baked-in -md remained and aborted the server at startup.

Make has_dft() additionally require that an enabled speculative type
actually consumes a draft model (draft-simple, draft-eagle3, draft-mtp).
Both call sites (draft-model load and --fit VRAM reservation in
server-context.cpp) want exactly this semantic.

diff --git a/common/common.h b/common/common.h
index 13f3872..043a41f 100644
--- a/common/common.h
+++ b/common/common.h
@@ -358,7 +358,15 @@ struct common_params_speculative {
     common_params_speculative_ngram_cache ngram_cache;
 
     bool has_dft() const {
-        return !draft.mparams.path.empty() || !draft.mparams.hf_repo.empty();
+        // a configured draft model counts only if an enabled speculative type
+        // will actually consume it (e.g. --spec-type none must win over a
+        // baked-in -md, see llamafile .args)
+        const bool wants_draft_model = std::any_of(types.begin(), types.end(), [](auto t) {
+            return t == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_SIMPLE ||
+                   t == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_EAGLE3 ||
+                   t == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP;
+        });
+        return wants_draft_model && (!draft.mparams.path.empty() || !draft.mparams.hf_repo.empty());
     }
 
     uint32_t need_n_rs_seq() const {
